diff --git a/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md b/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md
index ce84761..3051721 100644
--- a/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md
+++ b/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md
@@ -32,3 +32,33 @@ The system SHALL provide a sort control on the search page that allows the user
 - **WHEN** the user changes sort and navigates to a book detail page and back
 - **THEN** the sort control SHALL still show the previously selected sort option
 - **THEN** the results SHALL be served from cache (no new network request)
+
+---
+
+### Requirement: User can filter search results by author
+
+The system SHALL provide an author filter on the search page with an accessible label "Author:". The control SHALL list "All authors" (empty value) followed by the distinct author names present in the current results. Selecting an author SHALL refetch results with Open Library's `author` parameter, reset pagination to the first page, and show only books by that author. Selecting "All authors" SHALL clear the filter and restore the unfiltered results. Search input, sort, and Load more behavior SHALL remain unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Author filter lists authors from current results
+
+- **WHEN** search results are displayed
+- **THEN** the author control SHALL show "All authors" as the selected default option
+- **THEN** it SHALL list each distinct author name from the loaded results exactly once
+
+#### Scenario: User filters by author
+
+- **WHEN** the user selects an author from the author control
+- **THEN** the system SHALL refetch results with the `author` query parameter set to the selected name
+- **THEN** pagination SHALL reset to page 1
+- **THEN** the results grid SHALL only show books by the selected author
+
+#### Scenario: User clears the author filter
+
+- **WHEN** the user selects "All authors"
+- **THEN** the system SHALL clear the author filter
+- **THEN** the results grid SHALL show the unfiltered result set
+
+#### Scenario: Author filter is hidden without results
+
+- **WHEN** there are no results (empty state, error, or no query)
+- **THEN** the author filter SHALL NOT be visible
